  "tutorialTitle": "How the app works",
  "tutorialPage1Title": "How Vokabeltrainer works",
  "tutorialPage1Text": "This app helps you learn vocabulary in any language – with flashcards, tests and smart review. Swipe left or tap “Next” to see everything.",
  "tutorialPage2Title": "Create a lesson",
  "tutorialPage2Text": "In the “Lessons” tab you create a lesson: name, language and what you want to learn – word and translation, plus forms and up to three of your own fields like example sentence or memory aid if you want.",
  "tutorialPage3Title": "Scan words",
  "tutorialPage3Text": "Type in the words yourself – or tap “Scan” and take a photo of the list in your book. An AI app like ChatGPT or Gemini reads it. Copy its answer, come back, done.",
  "tutorialPage4Title": "Create practice lists",
  "tutorialPage4Text": "On the home screen, tap “Practice lists” and then “New list”. Give the list a name, optionally the date of your vocab test, and pick the words from your lessons.",
  "tutorialPage5Title": "Study every day",
  "tutorialPage5Text": "On the home screen, “Today” shows what's up next from your lists: due reviews first, plus up to 15 new words. Tap “Let's go” to start.",
  "tutorialPage6Title": "Flashcards",
  "tutorialPage6Text": "Tap the card to flip it and rate yourself honestly: “Again”, “Hard”, “Good” or “Easy”. Under each button you can see when the card comes back. On a computer: space to flip, 1–4 to rate.",
  "tutorialPage7Title": "Smart review",
  "tutorialPage7Text": "The app asks you each word right before you'd forget it (spaced repetition with FSRS, like Anki). Words you know well come up less often, tricky ones more often. Study a little every day – that keeps your 🔥 streak alive.",
  "tutorialPage8Title": "Your vocab test in sight",
  "tutorialPage8Text": "When you create a list, enter the date of your test. The app spreads the new words over the days so you're done the day BEFORE the test – that's when everything gets reviewed once more. The closer the test, the more often the words come up.",
  "tutorialPage9Title": "Reminders",
  "tutorialPage9Text": "The app reminds you up to 3 times a day – with up-to-date numbers and never after 9 pm. Once you're done for the day, they stop. You can change this under Settings → Reminders.",
  "tutorialPage10Title": "Test mode",
  "tutorialPage10Text": "Here you type in the translation and/or the forms yourself – and your own fields too if you want (Settings). When checking, upper/lower case and articles (like “the” or “a”) don't matter.",
  "tutorialPage11Title": "See your progress",
  "tutorialPage11Text": "In the “Analysis” tab you see every word with its learning level: 5 shades of green (good), gray (neutral) and 5 shades of red (weak). Tap a word for its history chart and to make it better or worse by hand with +/−.",
  "tutorialPage12Title": "Your data",
  "tutorialPage12Text": "Everything is saved only on this device – no account, no internet. Make a backup in the settings every now and then. You can also use it to move to another device.",
